 <h1>Exercise Name: Seated Dumbbell Wrist Curl (Underhand Wrist Curl)</h1>
        <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u>
  Exercise Name: Seated Dumbbell Wrist Curl (Underhand Wrist Curl)
  Target Muscles: Forearm Flexors (Flexor Carpi Radialis & Flexor Carpi Ulnaris) and Grip Muscles
  Visual Description: A 3D animated figure is seated on a gym bench with forearms resting on the thighs, holding a dumbbell. As the wrist curls upward, the forearm flexor muscles highlight in red, showing the exact area being targeted during the movement.</p>
 </div></div>


 <h1>è Step-by-Step Instructions</h1>

<u><b><h4>1. Setup:</h4></b></u>
 Sit near the edge of a flat bench with your feet firmly planted on the ground, shoulder-width apart.
 Hold a dumbbell in your hand using an underhand grip (palms facing upward).
 Rest your forearm along your thigh so that your wrist extends just beyond your knee.


<u><b><h4>2. Lowering (Eccentric Phase):</h4></b></u>
 Slowly lower the dumbbell toward the floor by flexing your wrist downward.
 Allow the weight to roll slightly into your fingers at the bottom for a full stretch, maintaining control throughout.


<u><b><h4>3. Curling (Concentric Phase):</h4></b></u>
 Curl the dumbbell upward as high as possible using only your wrist joint.
 Pause briefly at the top of the movement and squeeze your forearm muscles tightly.


<u><b><h4>4. Lowering Back Down:</h4></b></u>
 Controlled and slow return to the starting position. Avoid rushing or bouncing the weight.





<h1> Benefits</h1>

 <b>Forearm Growth & Aesthetics:</b> Directly isolates and builds the inner forearms for a balanced arm look.
 <b>Improved Grip Strength:</b> Enhances functional grip strength, which transfers directly to heavy compound exercises like deadlifts, pull-ups, and heavy rows.
 <b>óâWrist Stability:</b> Fortifies the tendons and muscles around the wrist joint, helping prevent strain and joint injury during heavy training.



<h1> Recommended Sets & Reps</h1>

| Goal | Sets | Repetitions | Rest Interval |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Growth (Hypertrophy) | 3 ‚Äì 4 | 12 ‚Äì 15 reps | 45 ‚Äì 60 seconds |
